# Build a personal study-buddy flashcard page in 15 minutes with Hugging Face Spaces

> **In short:** You'll create a free **Static Space** on Hugging Face and paste in one ready-made `index.html` file. It shows your flashcards one by one: you think of the answer, reveal it, and mark **I knew it** or **Not yet**. Cards you don't know yet come back until you've got them all.

Flashcards work best when you test yourself instead of just rereading notes. This guide gives you a small quiz page you can open on any device with a browser. To be clear about what it is: it's a simple page that runs your own cards. It doesn't use an AI model, and it doesn't make up questions for you, so every answer it shows is one you wrote.

## Before you start

- **A Hugging Face account.** Sign up at [huggingface.co](https://huggingface.co) if you don't have one.
- **Know what's free.** Hugging Face's docs say Static Spaces are free for everyone and never need a paid plan. (Gradio and Docker Spaces, which run on compute, need a paid plan to create, so this guide uses a Static Space.)
- **A few questions you want to learn,** each with a short answer.
- **About 15 minutes.** You won't write code yourself: you'll copy one file and change only the question and answer text.

## Step 1: Create a new Space

Go to [huggingface.co/spaces](https://huggingface.co/spaces) and click **Create new Space** (or open [huggingface.co/new-space](https://huggingface.co/new-space) directly). Fill in the form:

- **Name:** something short, such as `my-study-buddy`. It becomes part of your Space's address.
- **License:** optional. You can leave it empty.
- **SDK:** choose the **static HTML** option.
- **Visibility:** **Public** lets anyone with the link open your page. **Private** keeps the page and its files visible only to you (other people get a "404" error). Hugging Face notes that **Protected** is part of paid plans.

Then create the Space.

You'll know it worked when you're taken to your new Space's page, with tabs such as **Files**.

## Step 2: Add the quiz file

Hugging Face's docs say a Static Space serves the HTML in a file called **index.html**. To add it in your browser, open the **Files** tab and click **Add file**, then choose to create a new file. Name it `index.html`.

If an `index.html` file is already listed in your Space, open that file and replace everything in it instead.

You'll know it worked when you see an editor where you can name the file and type its content.

## Step 3: Paste the ready-made code

Copy this whole block and paste it into the file:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>My Study Buddy</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 560px; margin: 40px auto; padding: 0 16px; }
  #card { border: 2px solid #ccc; border-radius: 12px; padding: 24px; min-height: 120px; }
  #answer { margin-top: 16px; }
  button { font-size: 16px; padding: 10px 16px; margin: 12px 8px 0 0; cursor: pointer; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h2>📚 My Study Buddy</h2>
<p id="progress"></p>
<div id="card">
  <strong id="question"></strong>
  <div id="answer" hidden></div>
</div>
<button id="show">Show answer</button>
<button id="knew" hidden>I knew it</button>
<button id="again" hidden>Not yet</button>

<script>
// Your flashcards: ["question", "answer"]. Change, add, or delete lines.
const CARDS = [
  ["What do plants make during photosynthesis?", "Sugar and oxygen, using sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide."],
  ["What is the Spanish word for \"apple\"?", "la manzana"],
  ["What is 7 × 8?", "56"],
];

const queue = CARDS.slice();
for (let i = queue.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {
  const j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));
  [queue[i], queue[j]] = [queue[j], queue[i]];
}
let known = 0;
const el = (id) => document.getElementById(id);

function showCard() {
  if (queue.length === 0) {
    el("question").textContent = "Done! You knew all " + CARDS.length + " cards. Reload the page to start again.";
    el("answer").hidden = true;
    el("show").hidden = el("knew").hidden = el("again").hidden = true;
    el("progress").textContent = "";
    return;
  }
  el("question").textContent = queue[0][0];
  el("answer").textContent = queue[0][1];
  el("answer").hidden = true;
  el("show").hidden = false;
  el("knew").hidden = el("again").hidden = true;
  el("progress").textContent = "Known: " + known + " / " + CARDS.length;
}

el("show").onclick = () => {
  el("answer").hidden = false;
  el("show").hidden = true;
  el("knew").hidden = el("again").hidden = false;
};
el("knew").onclick = () => { queue.shift(); known++; showCard(); };
el("again").onclick = () => { queue.push(queue.shift()); showCard(); };

showCard();
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

At the bottom of the editor, save the file to the `main` branch (you can add a short message, such as "Add quiz page"). Hugging Face's docs say your Space rebuilds and restarts automatically each time you save a change.

You'll know it worked when `index.html` appears in your Space's file list.

## Step 4: Try your flashcards

Open your Space's page (the **App** view). You'll see one question. Think of the answer, then click **Show answer**.

- Click **I knew it** to remove the card from this round.
- Click **Not yet** to send it to the back of the line. It will come back.

When every card is marked **I knew it**, the page says you're done. Reload the page to start a new round.

You'll know it worked when the counter at the top goes up each time you click **I knew it**.

## Step 5: Put in your own questions

Open `index.html` again from the **Files** tab and edit the lines between `const CARDS = [` and `];`. Each card is one line in this shape:

```text
  ["Your question?", "Your answer"],
```

Keep the quotation marks, the comma between question and answer, and the comma at the end of the line. If your text needs a quotation mark inside it, put a backslash in front of it (`\"`), as in the "apple" example. Save the file again, and your Space updates.

💬 Example:
> ["What is the capital of Canada?", "Ottawa"],

You'll know it worked when your own questions show up after you reload the page.

## Common mistakes

- **The page is blank after an edit.** A missing quotation mark or comma in a card line usually causes this. Compare your line with the shape in Step 5, or paste the original code again.
- **Others can't open your link.** If your Space is private, only you can see it. You can change visibility later from your Space's **Settings** tab.
- **Expecting progress to be saved.** The page doesn't remember results between visits. Reloading starts a new round.
- **Expecting it to write questions for you.** It only shows the cards you typed. If you want help drafting questions, write them first with an AI assistant, check them yourself, then paste them in.

## What this means for you

- **In everyday life:** Practice vocabulary, dates, or formulas on your phone in short sessions.
- **For your business or work:** Put product facts or safety steps on cards so new team members can quiz themselves. Keep the Space private if the content is internal.
- **If you're just getting started:** This is a low-risk first project on Hugging Face: one file, free hosting, and nothing to install.

## Try it now

Create the Space, paste the code, and replace the three sample cards with five questions from whatever you're studying this week. Then go through one round and see how many you knew on the first try.
